{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton"]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","title":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton"}],"externalID":"s:5Tries20AhoCorasickAutomatonV","modules":[{"name":"Tries"}],"role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton.swift#L29","fileName":"AhoCorasickAutomaton.swift"}},"abstract":[{"text":"An automaton that finds every occurrence of every pattern of a set in one pass over a text","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(Aho and Corasick, 1975).","type":"text"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Tries\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It is the trie of the patterns with two more links per state: the failure link, to the state","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the longest proper suffix of the state’s prefix that is also a prefix of some pattern, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the output link, to the nearest state along the failure links at which a pattern ends. A scan","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"follows the trie while the text matches and the failure links where it stops matching, so it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reads each symbol of the text once and reports all the matches in O(","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"t","type":"text"}]},{"text":" + ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"k","type":"text"}]},{"text":") for a text of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"t"}]},{"text":" symbols with ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"k","type":"text"}]},{"text":" matches.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let automaton = AhoCorasickAutomaton(patterns: [\"he\", \"she\", \"his\", \"hers\"])","for match in automaton.matches(in: \"ushers\") {","    print(match.patternIndex, match.range)","}","\/\/ 1 1..<4   (\"she\")","\/\/ 0 2..<4   (\"he\")","\/\/ 3 2..<6   (\"hers\")"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Matches come in order of where they end, and of those ending at one place, longest first.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Ranges count the text’s symbols from 0. The automaton is built once and is immutable.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Symbols are mapped to dense indices at construction, through a 256-entry table when they are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UInt8"},{"type":"text","text":" and a dictionary otherwise, so a scan over bytes, such as a string’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"utf8"},{"type":"text","text":", does no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hashing. When the states times the distinct symbols are few enough, every transition is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"precomputed into a table, and a scan takes one load per symbol."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/Match","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/MatchesView","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/StatesView-swift.struct"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures"},{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/init(patterns:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/patternCount","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/stateCount","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/statesView-swift.property"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/containsMatch(in:)","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/firstMatch(in:)","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/matches(in:)","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/patternLength(at:)","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/patternLength(checkedAt:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://Tries/s8SendableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/s8SendableP","title":"Swift.Sendable","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton/firstMatch(in:)":{"type":"topic","title":"firstMatch(in:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documen